engine/godot/issues/comments/3426724976","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111882#issuecomment-3426724976","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111882","id":3426724976,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7MP6xw","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-21T13:39:16Z","updated_at":"2025-10-21T13:39:16Z","body":"This might not be a bug, this could be an intentional limitation of what the editor should suggest because of how safe or unsafe it is to use these methods as default values, most of the time they don't make much sense used that way, in fact the results are limited to static members and methods, as well as global methods and types, so this does seem intentional\n\nThe reason it \"works\" with `self` is that `self` overrides a lot of safety, so the fact that this changes when using `self` implies to me that this is an intentional limitation to prevent incorrect use, and that this safety is overridden or ignored by `self`\n\nBut will see what the GDScript team say, it at least should work differently for `@onready` variables where it *is* safe","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3426724976/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3426743567","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111882#issuecomment-3426743567","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111882","id":3426743567,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7MP_UP","user":{"login":"MadeScientist","id":190612698,"node_id":"U_kgDOC1yE2g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/190612698?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist","html_url":"https://github.com/MadeScientist","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-21T13:42:29Z","updated_at":"2025-10-21T13:46:00Z","body":"> This might not be a bug, this could be an intentional limitation of what the editor should suggest because of how safe or unsafe it is to use these methods as default values, most of the time they don't make much sense used that way, in fact the results are limited to static members and methods, as well as global methods and types, so this does seem intentional\n> \n> The reason it \"works\" with `self` is that `self` overrides a lot of safety, so the fact that this changes when using `self` implies to me that this is an intentional limitation to prevent incorrect use, and that this safety is overridden or ignored by `self`\n\nThat sounds very reasonable. Just like `self` doesn't pre-check whether the member name exists before running.\n\n> But will see what the GDScript team say, it at least should work differently for `@onready` variables where it _is_ safe\n\nExactly, this protection conflicts with the convenience provided by the onready variable.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3426743567/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3428984876","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111882#issuecomment-3428984876","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111882","id":3428984876,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7MYigs","user":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-21T19:09:44Z","updated_at":"2025-10-21T19:09:44Z","body":"I mean the code looks a bit like it's meant as protection but to me it looks quite overprotective. It treats variable initializers like a static context.\n\nThe code seems to predate 4.x so the intentions aren't that clear anymore and I would not read too much into it. We should start from how we want it to behave right now with the current features and state of GDScript.\n\nOnly suggesting static stuff outside of functions seems pretty useless to me because it disregards a lot of common usecases. There is no labeling regarding what can be used safely outside of `onready` (besides get node literals which are a well defined language feature). So implementing safeguards for that seems like a lot of work, it does not seem worth it to me.\n\nIMO we can just treat initializers like a non static context. Just needs some checking on how well our code paths work in cases were `current_scope` is `nullptr`.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3428984876/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3430886258","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111882#issuecomment-3430886258","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111882","id":3430886258,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Mfyty","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-22T07:48:25Z","updated_at":"2025-10-22T07:48:25Z","body":"To me, this looks like a bug, even if this restriction was intentional. Yes, avoiding non-pure or at least overly complex initializers is a good practice. But I don't think limiting it at the autocompletion level is the right solution. This problem should be addressed at the documentation level and through warnings (where possible and justified, as in the case of the `GET_NODE_DEFAULT_WITHOUT_ONREADY` warning).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3430886258/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]